# lib/ and lib64/ are what a virtualenv created in place (`python -m venv .`)
# leaves behind. Anchored to the two places that could happen, the repo root
# and backend/ (#327): a bare `lib/` matched every lib/ directory in the repo
# and silently dropped source files. The real venv, backend/venv/, is covered
# by venv/ above.
/lib/
/lib64/
/backend/lib/
/backend/lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
